set baselines** — *assumed* {0.001, 0.005, 0.01}; please confirm floors.\\n10. **`max_itemset_size` cap** — *assumed* {2, 3, 4}; please confirm.\\n11. **Split ratio and stratification** — *assumed* 70/30 stratified by target when available; please confirm.\\n12. **Seed set** — *assumed* {0, 1, 2, 3, 4}; please confirm.\\n13. **What counts as a \\\"metric\\\" for evaluation of an unlabeled natural dataset** — *assumed* the synthetic-injection precision/recall/F1@k and the null-control rate are the primary metrics, because there is no ground truth on a real dataset without labels; please confirm.\\n14. **Whether runtime measurement should also report memory** — *assumed* wall-clock only, because `psutil` is not guaranteed. *needs confirmation* if memory is required.\\n15. **Whether `track.md` is somewhere other than the literal `/workspace`** — *cannot be derived from supplied docs*. I only see the one-line string inside `task.json`.\\n16. **Software environment outside stdlib** — *assumed* pandas/numpy/sklearn/mlxtend available outside the sandbox; the design degrades to a stdlib-only subset if they are not.\\n17. **Reporting format** — *needs confirmation*. Default: one Markdown table per pattern family, plus a stability/seed-sweep table, plus a feasibility note.\\n18. **Whether to score rare patterns jointly vs. per-row** — *assumed* both: itemset scoring for R1/R2/R3 plus per-row anomaly scoring for sanity; please confirm.\\n\\nWhen you confirm or correct items 1–7 (the ones labelled `needs confirmation` that shape the result), I will expand the same three-section design into a full `stage=result` write-up — still design-only, no claimed run.\",\"evidence\":\"Inspection evidence:\\n- `ls -la /workspace` shows the only entry is `-rw------- task.json`; no `track.md` exists as a file.\\n- `find / -maxdepth 4 -iname \\\"docta*\\\"` returns nothing; `find / -maxdepth 4 -iname \\\"track.md\\\"` returns nothing.\\n- `cat /workspace/task.json` exposes `documents.track.md 